    "body": "## Summary\n- add secure job attachments with Flyway V37 metadata and an opaque storage abstraction\n- encrypt every stored object with AES-256-GCM before it reaches the filesystem\n- add a persistent Compose attachment volume without exposing filesystem paths or storage keys through the API\n- validate bounded file bytes by magic signature instead of trusting client MIME/extension; allow JPG/PNG/WebP/PDF only\n- enforce 10 MiB/file and configurable per-job count limits at application level plus a database size check\n- add `JOB_VIEWERS`, `PARTICIPANTS` and short-lived `EXECUTION_SECRET` visibility policies\n- keep `EXECUTION_SECRET` readable to the requester and only to the selected worker while the job is exactly `IN_PROGRESS`\n- revoke worker secret access on completion request/dispute/done/cancel without changing job/payment/location state\n- let the requester delete execution secrets at any time while regular transaction attachments become immutable after worker assignment\n- align open-job attachment visibility with bilateral user-block/public-detail policy\n- make uploads/deletes transaction-aware so failed database transactions clean up newly stored objects and committed tombstones remove ciphertext afterward\n- serve downloads as attachment/no-store/nosniff and never expose SHA/storage/encryption internals\n- add focused crypto/file/access/service tests and a real container multipart/encryption/lifecycle smoke\n\n## Product intent\n`JOB_VIEWERS` is suitable for a shopping list or product photo that candidates may need before accepting/proposing. `PARTICIPANTS` is private transaction material after assignment. `EXECUTION_SECRET` is specifically designed for temporary execution aids such as a loyalty-card barcode or pickup credential; it is not for payment cards, passwords or identity documents.\n\n## Storage/security\nThe repository ships a clearly documented local/CI-only 32-byte AES key. Production must override `ATTACHMENT_ENCRYPTION_KEY_BASE64` using secret management. The binary domain depends on `AttachmentStorage`, so a later S3/MinIO adapter does not require changing attachment metadata or authorization contracts.\n\n## Migration ordering\nTracking destination arrival is V36 on master. Job attachment metadata is therefore V37; the branch is merged with the current master before validation so Flyway sees the exact production order.\n\n## Runtime validation\nThe new smoke creates a funded on-site job, uploads all three visibility classes, verifies pre-assignment privacy, checks the raw mounted secret object does not contain its plaintext marker, accepts the job, verifies the selected worker can decrypt the secret, requests completion and verifies secret access is immediately revoked while historical participant material remains available. It also verifies post-assignment immutability and requester secret deletion.\n\nDo not merge unless Maven verify, frontend verify, payments/web smoke checks and the full container runtime smoke are green on the latest head.",
